// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3808749289" "This hidden lab beneath the city streets is filled with stolen Crey equipment."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3235678697" "Circuit Red Omega"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3647250212" "Get ready to add {HeroName} to our project database."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1684593617" "This is going to be the end of you, {HeroName}!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2469414513" "Zeus Class Titan"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P427298558" "Location secure. Preparing to engage enemy."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2710267860" "Enemy Meta-human detected. Initiating combat."
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2577214769" "The way I see it, once these guys are online, we win."
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P506737755" "And no more shepherding metas. Ain't technology grand?"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2149386954" "It's {HeroName}! I knew something like this would happen!"
// Script Variable OBJECT_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2395087792" "Revenant Project equipment"
// Script Variable ACTOR_GUARDING_DIALOG :
"P1309197471" "We get this equipment set up, then we go into production."
// Script Variable ACTOR2_GUARDING_DIALOG :
"P1421659697" "On it."
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P457576625" "Stop {HeroName}! This project cannot fail!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Equipment 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P2991027296" "Revenant Project items to destroy"
// SingularDescription :
"P4118491047" "Destroy last of Revenant Project!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4035107868" "You raided the Malta lab and put a final end to the Revenant Hero Project."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4036496763" "Closure is a difficult thing to find in any business, {HeroName}, so you should enjoy it when you can. That Crey scientist has plea bargained his testimony for a reduced sentence, but I'll have someone watching him, just in case. <br><br>Indigo is working on bringing the Malta informant out of the cold and onto our side. Don't know how that will go, but she likes to have faith in people. It's an endearing quality of her personality. <br><br>Most importantly, The Revenant Hero project is finally over. You just filled in the grave and put flowers on the tombstone. Like I said, closure can be hard to find. Take a minute out an enjoy it. <br><br>It's interesting to think about how ferociously all of those people fought for control of the Revenant program. Now, I can see the tactical appeal of having disposable superhumans to do all of your dirty work, but I believe that if you're not willing to risk your life or what you hold dear to accomplish your goal, then maybe you should re-think what you really want. Power, control, security; all of those are just fancy ways of saying that you're afraid, and you want to not be afraid anymore. People will do a lot to avoid fear, even become the monsters they're afraid of. <br><br>I suppose I also believe, as Abraham Lincoln said, that 'As I would not be a slave, so I would not be a master.'"
// RandomFameString :
"P4089764934" "I heard that you finally finished some kind of weird Crey investigation, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ConvictMom 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P213392734" "Mrs. Boxer's story"
// DetailString :
"P2964280114" "After you rescued her from agents of the Malta Group, Candice Boxer told you: <br><br> I'm so glad you came and saved, me, {HeroName}. All of this trouble started when I stopped hearing from my son, Joe. Joe was in prison, you see. Much as a mother hates to say it, my Joe wasn't always a good boy. Drugs, gangs, and worse. He broke my heart for many years. My only comfort was that he never got in with anything really horrid, like the Freakshow. This latest time, though, I think he was turning things around. He was trying to finish his high school degree in Ziggursky, and he wanted to be part of his son's life. He wrote me every week, and my heart was full of hope for the first time in may years. <br><br>But then the letters stopped. I didn't think too much of it at first, but then I tried to visit him, and no one in the Ziggursky administration had heard of my son. He wasn't in any of the prison records, even! I started to snoop around a bit, when a guard who'd always been nice told me that a new government contractor had taken over record keeping at Ziggursky. I tried to get my son's records from them, but they said I'd need a court order. Well, I was going to do just that, but then these men came. They took me from my home, and I think they were going to kill me to keep me quiet! <br><br>Oh, {HeroName}, I know you must hear these stories every day. My boy Joe wasn't an angel, but I'm very worried about him. Perhaps you could check in with that contractor, Prison Control Handling, and see what's happened to my son?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - TransferRecords 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3388069942" "Prisoner transfer records"
// DetailString :
"P2670677770" "You found these papers in the offices of Prison Control Handling, a government contractor who was helping to manage Ziggursky prison. Contrary to PCH's claims, you did find a reference to Mrs. Boxer's son. It seems that he and several other prisoners were transferred to an unspecified medical facility for some kind of operation. The medical records show that the men were all sedated to prevent escape attempts, so it seems unlikely that this operation was voluntary. <br><br>While the address of the facility isn't mentioned, it seems that the driver must have gotten lost on the way. There's a small map to the facility drawn on the copy of the transfer receipt."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PrisonerBrains 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2177517070" "Grim specimens"
// DetailString :
"P2751078227" "You found the gruesome sight inside this refrigerated container in a secret Malta Group lab that was producing Titan robots. Rack upon rack of disembodied human brains and nervous systems, each suspended in an individual container of sustaining bio-gel and labeled with a name and date of acquisition. The container marked 'Boxer, J.' is empty, as were several others."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - TitanControls 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2647778037" "Titan control schematics"
// DetailString :
"P1925278614" "You found these technical drawings on a computer in a Malta Group lab. They show how the Malta Group's Titan combat robots are controlled. The first and most disturbing thing you see is that the Titans aren't robots at all, but cyborgs that use a human brain to augment their battle computers. The computers, in turn, condition the brain to keep it in line. <br><br>Curiously, some of the notation in the margins of scanned images are in Cyrillic."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3903940326" "I got a perfect piece of heroing for you, {HeroName}. The Malta Group are about to get rid of a mother with a story to tell by the name of Candice Boxer. If you can save her life, you might want to listen to what she has to say. It seems that Mrs. Boxer got a little too close to something bad while she was looking for her son, Joe. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Now that she's crossed the Malta Group, she's going to need a rescue just to stay alive, much less to find her boy.</A> Let me give you a fair warning: This might not look like much, but this could get pretty tough before it's all done."
// AcceptString :
"P1611749887" "Rescue Candice Boxer from the Malta Group"
// SendOffString :
"P3612461145" "If you can save Mrs. Boxer and listen to what she has to say, this could lead to something big. I trust you'll be able to follow up."

