// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - RiktiMoved 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1132403350" "New Orders"
// DetailString :
"P2155930296" "You found this print-out of an email to Babel Red Beta, the leader of the Malta Group Operations team who had kidnapped Earth's negotiator with the Traditionalist Rikti. The orders state that Babel Red Beta's counterpart, Babel Red Alpha, is to move up his schedule and kill the Rikti Traditionalist negotiator, a scientist called C'Kelkah, ahead of schedule at a specified location."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P315643564" "Indigo's uncovered a situation that could be disastrous if allowed to proceed unchecked. It involves the Rikti, who aren't exactly my favorite people; and it involves the Malta Group. If there's any good point, it's that this situation she's discovered has more to do with mutual annihilation between the two groups than holding hands around a campfire. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>That's about all I can tell you; Indigo will be able to tell you the rest if you want to follow up.</A> <br><br>I'll warn you, though, Indigo thinks that this one might end up as a battle against time. Once you've made a move, Malta may try to act fast to keep you from winning the second round of this one. You've been warned."
// AcceptString :
"P2173435255" "Find out about the Malta Group/Rikti situation from Indigo"
// SendOffString :
"P3966543537" "Indigo should be waiting to talk to you. You'll probably have to see her in person. She'll have further instructions for you then."
// TaskTitle :
"P4275486162" "The Rikti Negotiator "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound3_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1846755776" "I'm glad to see you, {HeroName}. I think you're just the person to help handle this. <br><br>I don't know what you know about the current state of Rikti affairs, but the Rikti trapped on Earth seem to be factionalizing around different philosophies. I don't know the whole run-down of how and why it happened, but the two factions call themselves the Traditionalists and the Restructurists. The important thing is that the Traditionalists are willing to talk cease-fire, and our government has been trying to work one out with that faction. <br><br>This is where our 'friends' come in. They're planning to sabotage the talks. They've kidnapped two of the negotiators, one human and one Rikti, and are going to pin their deaths on the other side. Understanding why is part of their weird psychology. As far as our 'friends' are concerned, they would rather have an enemy they can make people afraid of and rally against, than a possible friend. From their point of view, it's safer and more useful for their own agenda if they have hostile Rikti aliens as a threat they can pull out at any time to scare people. If we had a cease-fire, that might lead to peace, or worse. <br><br>I don't know how you feel about the Rikti, but I think you can agree that preventing our 'friends' from using them as a boogey man is a good thing. So, I'm going to give you the locations of where they're holding both negotiators. The first one is Dr. Helen Spendler. I'll show you where our 'friends' are keeping her."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound3_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3340924036" "Defeat lead kidnapper & his men"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4284484260" "Indigo's got the right idea on this one. I've got no love for the Rikti, but I can see that keeping negotiations with these Traditionalists going is a good idea. You'll need to rescue Dr. Helen Spendler. Taking out her captors is probably a good idea while you're at it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P56842579" "The Malta Group has re-conditioned this abandoned Council base."
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3433213645" "When do we put that traitor Spendler out of our misery?"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1325627382" "Peace with the Rikti. The thought makes me sick."
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P432568739" "It's {HeroName}! How did that mask find us?"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2886320035" "Babel Red Beta"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P771766963" "We've had to move up the time table. Alpha's team is moving C'Kelkah."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3611556643" "Your interference ends here, {HeroName}."

