"P3172952603" "Surface to air missiles"
// Description :
"P3042553812" "missiles to find"
// SingularDescription :
"P726878501" "Find the last crate of missiles!"
// InteractBeginString :
"P2673744019" "You begin destroying the missiles."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P3741677091" "You have destroyed the missiles."
// InteractActionString :
"P3365161279" "Destroying..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3931877108" "You stopped Malta in time and saved the passenger liner. You also found some orders with interesting implications."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1708028781" "Despite your efforts, the Malta Group was able to shoot down the jet liner. However, you did find a set of orders for the Malta operatives with interesting implications."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound6_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2331431988" "Arrest airplane attack commander"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P576188195" "Those orders seem to point you to the right place to go. Look for the person responsible for the attack on that jet there."
// Script Variable LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P1914166542" "Our orders say you need to be dissuaded, {HeroName}!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2095865685" "The creaking ceiling of this old warehouse indicates its state of disrepair. "
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P573507993" "Knight Red 0-1"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2050952634" "I must not be captured by {HeroName}!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P636511870" "You'll get no answers from me, {HeroName}!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1794878453" "Who is that Knight Red 0-1 guy?"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P715224525" "Everyone seems to obey him. It's probably classified."
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3086457834" "It's {HeroName}! Inform Knight Red 0-1!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Computer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P1063295874" "Knight Red 0-1's Computer"
// Description :
"P2695665806" "Find information"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4259989526" "The contents of this laptop have been encrypted."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3172519906" "You defeated Knight Red 0-1 and found a laptop full of encrypted information."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound6_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1920089928" "Take laptop to Indigo"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1157558989" "Indigo might be able to make something of that laptop."
// Script Variable LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P1051085830" "There's {HeroName}. We have our orders."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4039657631" "Crimson told me you were coming, {HeroName}. Let me take a look at that laptop. <br><br>Clever, but nothing I can't handle. Give me a second. Oh, while I'm working, Crimson asked me to research a group called the 'Knights of Malta.' Turns out that our Malta Group weren't the first ones to use the Island of Malta as a base. The Knights of Malta were supposedly a splinter group from the Knights Templar, which is another secret society. The Knights of Malta split off from the Templars over a question of what the group's purpose was. That was like in the 1600's. The Knights of Malta wanted to use their secret society to influence the rulers of Europe. Set themselves up as rulers from behind the scenes, that kind of thing. The Knights of Malta faded into history without having a big impact, and the Templars were declared heretics by the church and destroyed. <br><br>Got it!  <br><br>Whoah! <br>Crimson's gonna blow his top! This laptop has part of an organization chart and a mission timeline. These Knights of Malta guys have agents spread throughout the Malta Group! All of our work and someone's already gone ahead and infiltrated Malta! It makes me so mad. <br>Hmm, a lot of these guys are sleeper agents, long term covert infiltrators. They'd have to have been in place for decades. According to the timeline, they're planning on a big wake up, and soon. With their agents in place, they could take over the Malta Group and get their own private covert army! Unless we can stop them. <br><br>According to this, they're waiting for the go signal. Your presence at the airplane attack seems to have disrupted their time table, but as long as the signal isn't sent, their agents will wait for a while. I'm sending you in to take down the operative in charge of sending the activate signal, code-named Knight Blue 1-0. Defeat him and his people, and maybe we can avert this for a while."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound6_Part4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3468876178" "Defeat Knight Blue 1-0"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2192816830" "This is a temporary solution, but it's only because of luck and skill that we have the opportunity to stop this at all. If you defeat Knight Blue 1-0. Take him out and we'll stop this. The sleepers will go on sleeping."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P4275805450" "You push the implications of battling conspiracies within conspiracies to the back of your mind. Right now, you have a job to do."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3032984093" "Knight Blue 1-0"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2527791531" "Soon, now. Very soon."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2346299230" "Why must this city's heroes interfere in everything!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P478313180" "You defeated Knight Blue 1-0!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P797206708" "First thing: Good work. Those sleeper agents won't make a move until they get their go signals. The last thing the world needs is for one group of secret society megalomaniacs to come under the sway of another. Indigo and I will keep an eye on this situation. The list of infiltrators you found on that laptop isn't complete, so this might come back to haunt us. <br><br>Which brings up a point of concern. Indigo has a theory that Neil Macintosh, the MI6 spook who put together the original meeting on the Island of Malta that would form the Malta Group, was actually a part of the Knights of Malta. The possibility that leads to is that there have always been an unseen hand behind the scenes, guiding the creation and policies of the Malta Group. That, or it was meant to work that way and got out of their hands. Hence the heavy-handed tactic that set all of this off. <br><br>Speaking of which, though I'm not under any obligation to tell you this, I figure you've earned it. I found out who the Knights of Malta were trying to kill by shooting down that plane. Turns out it was someone Indigo has been trying to prove is one of the leaders of the Malta Group's 'new guard.' I have no doubt that he was the target of the attack. The worst part is, that guy wasn't even on the plane. He cancelled his flight at the last minute. I've told you before, these people are remorseless, {HeroName}. They were willing to kill all of those innocents just for one man, and that was only part of their larger plan. Don't forget that those are the kind of people we're fighting."
// RandomFameString :
"P2869184727" "I keep hearing that you're working on some big stuff, {HeroName}, but I never read about it in the papers."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound7 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CrackedMasks 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P848095737" "Cracked masks"
// DetailString :
"P3924838477" "These white porcelain masks are the type normally worn by members of the Carnival of Shadows. They've been cracked and broken in battle, and now posses none of their former powers."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Blades 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2752800929" "Artemis blades"
// DetailString :
"P1694598005" "These are the kind of blades normally used by the Knives of Artemis. You captured these blades in battle on Crimson's request."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Codes 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2575940418" "Enigmatic Codes"
// DetailString :
"P3515578474" "These codes consist of pages upon pages of long numbers, printed by an old dot-matrix printer on paper bearing what looks like a watermark and letterhead in Russian. The seal on the letterhead is that of the former Union of Soviet Socialist Republics."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2155005587" "I have an operation for you that involves doing some very mean things to some very mean people. I won't be able to explain much of the reason why to you, but it is for a good reason. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>So, if you feel up to causing a lot of trouble for people who deserve it, let me know.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P2263574599" "Cause trouble for deserving villains"
// SendOffString :
"P3991190170" "I knew you'd be interested. Okay, first off, you'll need these. They're masks, the kind that the Carnival of Shadows wears. These ones are broken, so they really aren't dangerous in themselves. Now that you have those, I am going to give you a location where the Knives of Artemis are getting together before an attack. I want you to defeat all of them there. Every last one. Then, leave a bunch of these masks around, and take several of those swords the Knives of Artemis use. After that, There's a second location where the Carnival of Shadows are scoping to set up some kind of event. Defeat all of them there and, you guessed it, leave some swords behind. Indigo should have the next part ready for you after that, so you'll need to meet with her."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound7_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2334358432" "Defeat all Knives in cave"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2385024718" "Defeat all members of the Knives of Artemis at their staging point. Once you've done that, collect their swords and leave the cracked masks I gave you lying around."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1103572774" "The occasional sound of a weapon being cleaned or readied echoes through the caverns."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3352366326" "You defeated all of the Knives of Artemis in the caves, took several of their signature blades, and left the cracked masks behind."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound7_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2706221006" "Defeat all carnies in warehouse"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P881880654" "Defeat all the circus people and leave a few swords behind."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3301623824" "This broken-down old warehouse seems like a strange place to hold any kind of function, but then, the Carnival of Shadows are strange people."
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1463405845" "Ah-hah-hah-ha!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P355262812" "Tell us why you attacked our sisters!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P191389626" "Stay out of this, {HeroName}!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2350600569" "Maid Murder 'Em"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2859049141" "Sister Maxina"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P124166605" "After defeating all members of the Carnival of Shadows on the scene, you left several Artemis blades around, as per Crimson's instructions. "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound7_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2578769726" "You've done an excellent job. Indigo has the third and final part of all this set up. Meet with her and she'll get everything ready."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1904069423" "The Knives of Artemis and the Carnival of Shadows have started fighting each other, thanks to your work. Those two groups don't have the friendliest relationship in the first place, so it should take them a while to calm down and figure out that neither of them started this. That should give us enough time for you to accomplish the whole goal of this operation. <br><br>With the Knives distracted, this is the first, best, and probably only opportunity to get a dangerous little something out of their possession. It's a series of files, codes actually, long numerical codes. The Knives got hold of them while on an operation for Malta in the Balkans, and they got a bit lost in the shuffle. With things disorganized, they could be taken from the Knives' without them ever realizing what they really are. Of course, I can't tell you what they're codes for, or what they could be used to, but it's important that neither the Knives nor their employers in Malta realize that they ever even had them. <br><br>I know where the codes are kept. Get them, and you can ignore as much as you can of what's going on between the Carnival and the Knives. <br>Well, I suppose you could spend some time feeling very satisfied, but you should keep your mind on the goal."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound7_Part4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P648934849" "Recover the codes"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P924723447" "You'll need to enter the Knives' base, find the codes, and remove them. Don't worry about anything else. Things should be pretty chaotic in there, but don't feel like you need to participate."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1768818033" "The women's screams you hear are not of terror, but of fury."
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2441514924" "We'll cut you freaks up!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1467018437" "So, {HeroName}, do you want some too?"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1164580597" "Just 'cause I'm pretty doesn't mean I'm not dangerous!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3659281389" "Sister Clarice"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2592055478" "The Captivating Christine"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P880250952" "Maybe not, if you knew how to fight!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2337135608" "You do not stand a chance"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2081940935" "This ends now."
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P763894984" "Sister Rachel"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_DISPLAYNAME :
"P927345590" "Illusionist"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P1801049261" "Sister Lilliana"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_DISPLAYNAME :
"P102367955" "Our Lady of Misery"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P831100641" "We'll show you stuck-up pretentious harlots the meaning of pain!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2481661534" "Do you think you can handle this, {HeroName}!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2450236546" "Oooh, tempting."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3657575170" "Sister Asheena"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P467351052" "Curse those pretentious sorority clowns! Why did they start this!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1106012893" "You can't be working for the carnies, {HeroName}. What are you here for? Tell me!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Boxes 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P1880109378" "Box of papers"
// Description :
"P519359192" "Find the codes"
// InteractBeginString :
"P620118964" "You begin searching the boxes."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P1627539300" "You finish searching the boxes."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1289851921" "You found the codes."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3128319876" "You recovered the codes from the Knives of Artemis."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P617573855" "Here are the masks. Don't worry, they lost all their power when they were broken."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4137455347" "I'll take those codes from you, {HeroName}. <br>Thank you. <br>Congratulations. You've just averted the biggest nuclear terrorist threat the world has ever seen. Those codes? Russian launch codes. Neither the Knives, nor Malta, nor even the Russians knew this copy survived, hidden in a vault for all of these years. Most of the Russian nukes have been decommissioned, now, but if these had worked on one in ten, well, let's just say that there would have been a lot more people applying at GIFT, or what was left of it. With the Knives and the Carnival fighting, it's unlikely that they'll miss one box of random numbers, meaning I can get it to the right people safely. So you see, it all went according to plan."
// RandomFameString :
"P2794907782" "Did you hear about how someone recovered all of these old Russian nuclear codes? Wow!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound8 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - NemesisToMalta 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2650727941" "Malta Group contracts"
// DetailString :
"P3686869305" "These papers are contracts for employment within the Malta Group. The contract specifically states that the person signing it will leave the Nemesis Army and give over all Nemesis technology they possess, along with any Nemesis Army related information, and in exchange receive a very well paid contract to work for the Malta Group."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - WearingWire 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1003353311" "Surveillance devices"
// DetailString :
"P155314300" "You found these surveillance devices on several of the Nemesis Army negotiators. These are clearly Nemesis technology, designed to record audio and video and send it back to another location. With a bit of work (and some quick calls to old contacts), you can trace the signal to its destination point."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MonitoredTalks 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3022385206" "Surveillance records"
// DetailString :
"P87605856" "You found dozens of different recordings made by Nemesis Army troops of their negotiations with Malta Group operatives. Each time, the Malta Group is trying to subvert the Nemesis troops into joining them. Each record is accompanied by a report by the Nemesis troops about how much the Malta Group negotiators believed them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - NemesisParts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1194198627" "Nemesis technology spare parts"
// DetailString :
"P809903169" "The spare parts you found seem almost puzzling at first. Though they're clearly Nemesis technology, they clearly aren't for repairing an automaton. In fact, they seem like just what you'd need to repair a biological support system that was based on Nemesis technology. Indigo's words return to mind. If Nemesis were alive, this would be the kind of plan he'd do. And if Nemesis were alive, he'd need parts like these to maintain his armor."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PlanOfAttack 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P454664989" "A plan of attack"
// DetailString :
"P912589036" "You found these meticulous battle plans in a Nemesis base. They note where a high-ranking Malta Group operative and cell leader will be going to conclude what he will believe to be a deal to annex a portion of the Nemesis Army. What he doesn't know is that he and his men will be the ones getting annexed by Nemesis!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P128069183" "All right, {HeroName}, I have an operation that I'm going to need your help with, but I have to warn you flat-out that this could be incredibly dangerous. Not that anything involving the Malta Group is ever safe and easy, but with the Nemesis Army involved, this could go above and beyond that. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>If you're up to it, I need your help to investigate what exactly the Malta Group and the Nemesis Army have to talk about.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P1832027316" "Investigate what the Malta Group and the Nemesis Army talking about"
// SendOffString :
"P2123128823" "I don't know if you're aware of the current state of the Nemesis Army, but they've taken a pretty bad blow. It looks like Nemesis is finally dead and gone, and most people expected them to just break up and go back to whatever life they led before. That hasn't been the case. They still perform operations and do missions and get orders, but no one really knows if those orders are coming from the Nemesis Army leadership and they've assumed command, or if they're coming from a usurper who's taken over as a new Nemesis, or from Nemesis himself. <br><br>Whatever the case is, despite those orders, some Nemesis Army troops are getting worried by these turns of events, and have been talking with representatives of, you guessed it, our friends in the Malta Group. So, what I want you to do is crash one of these little talks, defeat the negotiators, and try to find some clue over what all of this is about."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound8_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1985402168" "Defeat lead negotiators"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1108842078" "Once you're at the target location, you'll have two things to do. First, I want you to find out what the Nemesis Army and the Malta Group are talking about. This is the Nemesis Army, so I'm sure they'll be some paperwork around. Second, I want you to help derail those talks. Take out all of the negotiators."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2057523225" "Both the Malta Group and the Nemesis army are incredibly dangerous by themselves. Any potential alliance between them must be stopped."
// Script Variable NEGOTIATOR_ONE_INACTIVE_TEXT :
"P42510397" "It's clear that the Nemesis army is going nowhere. Join us."
// Script Variable NEGOTIATOR_TWO_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P3667154764" "We are espied upon!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2696199734" "Babel Green 2-4"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2503164605" "Negotiator Willcleff"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Desk 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P1491361393" "Paperwork"
// Description :
"P4006488557" "Find negotiation clues"
// InteractBeginString :
"P2623361317" "You begin searching the papers on the desk."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P3208860547" "You finish searching the papers."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2992964101" "You found documentation on the talks."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2102889084" "You disrupted the negotiations between this group of Nemesis Army soldiers and members of the Malta Group. You also found that several of the Nemesis Army soldiers were wearing recording devices."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound8_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3750279335" "Defeat monitoring station leader"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2950627065" "The trace you got is lucky, but it's clean. It should lead you to something interesting. You should concentrate on finding any and all records that were sent to that point, and on defeating whoever is in charge there."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P4215778891" "The signals you traced have led you here. Hidden in the city sewers, a gleaming high tech lab sprawls before you. All imprinted with the indelible mark of the Nemesis Army."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2050700384" "Fake Nemesis"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P4160888859" "Send the last of the information ahead. {HeroName} should be here soon."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3456847182" "Ah, {HeroName}. Welcome to your doom!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Computer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P912290260" "Monitoring station"
// Description :
"P1176173368" "recordings to find"
// SingularDescription :
"P1984084975" "Find the last recording"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1152823338" "You found recordings of Nemesis/Malta negotiations."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1622115343" "You shut down this monitoring station and got copies of all of their recordings. Indigo could probably help correlate them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound8_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2015914367" "Take recordings to Indigo"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1265731099" "Indigo is going to have a fun time with those recordings. She should be able to pull that information together into something you can use."
// Script Variable LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P3975669099" "You need to learn not to interfere with the Nemesis Army, {HeroName}!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2156689452" "Wow, {HeroName}, this is some juicy stuff. Give me moment to look through all of this. <br><br>Hmmm. <br><br>Interesting. <br><br>These are the weirdest time and date stamps. <br><br> Ah-ha! Okay! All of this data was being fed to a central point. My guess is that there are probably several monitoring stations like this one, all watching over Nemesis Army negotiation teams. I don't know if they're all talking to our 'friends', or if other groups are involved. A lot of villain organizations have been trying to move in on the Nemesis Army, now that it looks like Nemesis is gone. But seeing this effort on recording and analyzing, looking for other groups to show interest? This looks like part of a larger plan. <br><br>I'm like everyone else, {HeroName}. I really hope that Nemesis is gone forever. I know that we can't count on that. If this really is some elaborate plan to draw in and subvert other groups by tricking them into accepting Nemesis agents, then it can't be allowed to continue. I've been able to trace enough back that I should have the location of the central monitoring depository. I don't know what you'll find in there, but I'd really recommend that you take friends along."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound8_Part4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3586664546" "Find info at monitoring base"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2485109279" "This place could be extremely dangerous, {HeroName}. Your main goal is to try and find out whatever the Nemesis Army is up to so we can stop them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P968021904" "Indigo's information was correct once more. Hidden behind a facade of normal office space, you've found another secret Nemesis hideout!"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P87068466" "I report to you, Lord Nemesis, that I am ready to repel the foe!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2218968951" "And you would be {HeroName}? Excellent! Prepare to be destroyed!"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2518001440" "Ah, another visitor!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2490144028" "Stay awhile, {HeroName}. Stay forever!"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P267488499" "Lord Nemesis is at the scene. This will be over soon."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3729706128" "I'd offer you to join us, {HeroName}, but Lord Nemesis would be too satisfied by your death."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - NemesisRepair 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P3961196901" "Nemesis repair parts"
// InteractBeginString :
"P4018473916" "You begin to examine some Nemesis tech parts."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P2306172456" "You've finished examining the parts."
// InteractActionString :
"P1412195360" "Examining..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4137599212" "You found some interesting parts."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Computer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P2459521770" "Nemesis computer"
// Description :
"P480797583" "Seek clues"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4175611685" "You found copies of Nemesis' plans!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Malta_Compound8_Part5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P4128879608" "Stop Nemesis!"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P281690655" "I don't know if I can believe that Nemesis is back again. I just know that who or whatever is calling itself Nemesis has to be stopped. {HeroName}, I am entrusting that job to you. Indigo and I will try to get the word out."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2810966459" "It looks like the Malta Group operatives who'd come here expecting intense negotiations got an intense fire fight instead. They seem to be holding their own, but if Nemesis himself is truly here, it can't last."
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P4104520515" "Babel Red 8-7"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2858636606" "We've been out-maneuvered! Fall back!"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2579563041" "Warhulk"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3940184508" "Press the attack, men! For Lord Nemesis!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3075755256" "For Lord Nemesis!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3606259257" "We are being overrun! Send reinforcements!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2702427725" "It's {HeroName}! This just went from bad to worse!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P461145759" "Sapper"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P130938594" "Hercules Class Titan"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1692991500" "We can win this!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_ONE_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2835416100" "Don't give an inch!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3590122086" "You had best surrender now."
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P1963237575" "Babel Blue 9-6"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2731761601" "We offered you everything!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P34197774" "You can all die together!"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1577414093" "Lord Nemesis has already given me everything."
// Script Variable NEGOTIATOR_ONE_INACTIVE_TEXT :
"P1578329462" "You may take this cell, but the Malta Group will fight you forever!"
// Script Variable NEGOTIATOR_TWO_INACTIVE_TEXT :
"P2722416055" "And that sort of hubris is why I shall always win in the end. Let us discuss your surrender."
// Script Variable NEGOTIATOR_TWO_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P1058915009" "Ah, {HeroName}. Have we met? Or perhaps it was another, earlier Nemesis? Either way, I shall crush you and any companions this time."
// Script Variable BOSS_ONE_DISPLAYNAME :
"P1446221669" "Vital Gold 1-2-1"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3077890394" "Nemesis?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P129733148" "You have stopped the Nemesis Army's plot to infiltrate the Malta Group and defeated Nemesis. Or have you?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P110552163" "I told you that one was gonna be tough, but it looks like you handled it as well as anyone could have expected. The Malta Group's plan to subvert parts of the Nemesis Army is done with, as is the Nemesis Army's plan to subvert parts of the Malta Group. Vital Gold 1-2-1 is in custody, and that's a lot of damage to the Malta Cells in Paragon City. And then there's Nemesis. <br><br>Who or whatever was inside that Nemesis body was killed when you defeated it. Internal boilers went into the red, fried most everything. Indigo monitored the medical reports, and according to the doctors, while there was a brain in there, meaning that it could have been Nemesis himself, the brain was, well, artificial. Like one of the brains Crey was working on for the next step in the Revenant Hero project. All of which makes me wonder if that might have been not the real Nemesis, but a real Nemesis?"
// RandomFameString :
"P2771613206" "I heard the scariest thing today. Someone said Nemesis might still be alive. That isn't true, is it {HeroName}?"
